# Stone needs a wooden pickaxe or better; this skill builds the pickaxe if
# it has none. Depth 3: get_cobblestone -> get_wooden_pickaxe -> leaf. With the
# pickaxe in hand, no stone in reach means walking to a frontier of the
# perception known map first; without the pickaxe the wood chain comes first,
# because stone cannot be mined yet. Before that walk the body takes its placed
# table along: the wooden pickaxe leaves three planks, one short of a new table,
# and a body far from the trees then explored for one more log instead of
# crafting. This skill decides to leave, so the rule lives here, not in the
# caller (only the innermost frame selects a rule each tick).
skill get_cobblestone(n: int = 3)
  doc "Collect at least n cobblestone, crafting a wooden pickaxe first if needed."
  rules:
    count(cobblestone) >= $n -> done
    has(wooden_pickaxe) and not near(stone, 5) and near(crafting_table, 4) and not has(crafting_table) -> mine(crafting_table)
    has(wooden_pickaxe) and not near(stone, 5) -> explore(stone)
    has(wooden_pickaxe) -> mine(stone) until count(cobblestone) >= $n
    true -> do get_wooden_pickaxe()
